schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Wikipedia Good Article process requires a reviewer citation spot-check
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    To pass Wikipedia's Good Article process, an article must cite reliable
    sources inline for anything that could reasonably be challenged, and the
    reviewer does a spot-check — sampling citations and confirming each source
    actually supports the sentence it's attached to.
  evidence: >-
    Article cites "Wikipedia: Good Article criteria" (en.wikipedia.org) in its
    reference list as the source for this description.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/editorial-workflow.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's clearest real-world model for the claim-evidence
    discipline it recommends this commons adopt — held up as the example to
    emulate in the Review stage.
  uncertainty: >-
    Faithfully restates the article's own characterization of Wikipedia's
    process; not independently re-verified against Wikipedia's actual current
    Good Article criteria page in this ingest pass.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/editorial-workflow.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-379fb55cc1a6
